// The world: a region (one map), zones (where exploring finds things) and
// locations with exits. The validator checks that exits go both ways and that
// map positions don't overlap.

== region woods
name: The Quiet Woods
travel order: 1
map grid: 6 x 6

// A zone groups places for exploring. `ambient` lines show now and then while
// exploring; events and creatures name the zones they are found in.
== zone forest
name: The forest
ambient:
    Birds go quiet as you pass, then start up again behind you.

    Somewhere a branch cracks. Probably nothing.

    Sunlight flickers through the needles overhead.

== zone riverbank
name: The riverbank
ambient:
    The river chatters over stones.

    A heron lifts off from the shallows, slow and grey.

// `flags`: "known at start" (on the map from the start), "fast travel" (the
// player can travel here from any other fast travel point, and scavenge here),
// "safe rest". `rest:` is the bedding quality here.
== location cabin
name: Your Cabin
region: woods
zone: none
map: 2, 3
rest: bed
flags: safe rest, known at start, fast travel
items: wool_coat, bandage
exits:
    east: forest_path
    north: tool_shed, door shed_door
// Text can change with conditions: [if ...]...[else]...[end if], and with the
// player's content settings ("level detail is more").
description:
    A one-room cabin with a woodstove, a narrow bed and a window that sticks. [if time is night]The stove glows orange in the dark.[else]Sunlight falls in dusty stripes across the floor.[end if][if level detail is more] A row of jars on the shelf holds dried mint, nettles and something you can't name.[end if]
observe:
    * The window -- Look out of the window
        [weather]
    * The night -- Listen to the woods [if time is night]
        -> woods.night_sounds

// A door between two places, named in both places' exits ("door shed_door").
// `locked` can be yes, no or a condition.
== door shed_door
name: Shed door
locked: not player has shed_key
locked text: The shed door is padlocked. The key must be somewhere.
shown in room: A narrow door leads north to the tool shed.
description: A narrow plank door with a rusty padlock.

== location tool_shed
name: Tool Shed
region: woods
zone: none
map: 2, 2
items: boots
exits:
    south: cabin, door shed_door
description:
    Shelves of rusty tools and coils of rope. It smells of oil and old wood.

== location forest_path
name: Forest Path
region: woods
zone: forest
map: 3, 3
items: wild_berries
exits:
    west: cabin
    east: clearing
    south: old_bridge
description:
    A narrow path between tall pines. Needles soften every step. A fork leads south toward the sound of water.

== location clearing
name: Old Clearing
region: woods
zone: forest
map: 4, 3
flags: fast travel
exits:
    west: forest_path
description:
    A ring of mossy stones around a patch of open sky. Someone has built a lean-to at the edge.
// An observe menu: things the player can watch here (the Observe button).
observe:
    * The birds -- Watch the birds in the treetops
        A pair of jays squabble over a pinecone. [one of]The bigger one wins.[or]The smaller one wins, this time.[at random]
    * The sky -- Look up at the sky [if time is night]
        Stars, more than you've ever seen in town.

== location old_bridge
name: Old Bridge
region: woods
zone: riverbank
map: 3, 4
exits:
    north: forest_path
description:
    A mossy stone bridge over a quick, clear river. The far side is lost in mist.
